ull,"comments":11,"created_at":"2019-05-23T15:26:36Z","updated_at":"2019-09-02T10:37:34Z","closed_at":"2019-09-02T10:37:34Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Bug\r\n\r\nFor bugs/questions:\r\n* OS: macOS\r\n* Python version `import sys; print(sys.version)`: 3.7.1\r\n* Pydantic version `import pydantic; print(pydantic.VERSION)`: StrictVersion ('0.25')\r\n\r\nHere's a short example:\r\n\r\n```py\r\n>>> from pydantic import BaseModel, urlstr\r\n>>> class DatabaseConfig(BaseModel):\r\n...     url: urlstr(schemes={'postgresql'}, require_tld=False) = ...\r\n... \r\n>>> DatabaseConfig(url='postgresql://diary_test@localhost/diary_test')\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>\r\n  File \"pydantic/main.py\", line 235, in __init__\r\n    object.__setattr__(self, '__values__', self._process_values(data))\r\n  File \"pydantic/main.py\", line 438, in _process_values\r\n    return validate_model(self, input_data)  # type: ignore\r\n  File \"pydantic/main.py\", line 635, in validate_model\r\n    raise ValidationError(errors)\r\npydantic.error_wrappers.ValidationError: 1 validation error\r\nurl\r\n  url string does not match regex (type=value_error.url.regex)\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo, couple of problems:\r\n\r\n- This url is valid, it works ;-) \r\n- \"does not match regex\" isn't at all helpful to the end user, we should at least include the pattern being matched.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"samuelcolvin","id":4039449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMzk0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4039449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcolvin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sa